E78F 3606             (    forth6809.asm):04313                  PSHU  D          ; 10,S, which was itself wrong - it assumed
E791 39               (    forth6809.asm):04314                  RTS              ; DOSETUP's own JSR-pushed return address
                      (    forth6809.asm):04315                                   ; persists on S once each DOSETUP finishes.
                      (    forth6809.asm):04316                                   ; It doesn't: DOSETUP's own RTS pops and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04317                                   ; consumes it to jump into the loop body, so
                      (    forth6809.asm):04318                                   ; it never actually sits on S for J to count
                      (    forth6809.asm):04319                                   ; past. Re-traced by counting every real
                      (    forth6809.asm):04320                                   ; push/pop across a nested DO: after the
                      (    forth6809.asm):04321                                   ; inner DOSETUP finishes, S is [inner-index@0]
                      (    forth6809.asm):04322                                   ; [inner-limit@2][inner-leave@4][outer-
                      (    forth6809.asm):04323                                   ; index@6][outer-limit@8][outer-leave@10] -
                      (    forth6809.asm):04324                                   ; J's own JSR pushes one more cell on top,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04325                                   ; landing outer-index at 8, not 10. Offset 10
                      (    forth6809.asm):04326                                   ; read the outer loop's limit instead - a
                      (    forth6809.asm):04327                                   ; fixed value every iteration, exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):04328                                   ; matching the observed bug (J stuck at the
                      (    forth6809.asm):04329                                   ; limit, never progressing). Confirmed via a
                      (    forth6809.asm):04330                                   ; real MULT-TABLE test on MAME.
                      (    forth6809.asm):04331         
